<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salih ibn Mirdas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1029</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salih ibn Mirdas was an emir of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-kilab">Banu Kilab</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> who founded the Mirdasid dynasty. In 1024 he captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> from the Fatimid governor, ending the rule of the Lu'lu'id regents, and held much of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. He was killed in 1029 fighting the Fatimid army at al-Uqhuwana near Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberias">Tiberias</a>, but his sons kept Aleppo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salih-ibn-mirdas.jpg" alt="Salih ibn Mirdas" width="320" height="313" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Not credited · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Salih_ibn_Mirdas_gold_dinar_1028.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
